  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CitiesAdapt: strengthening climate change adaptation in cities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rapid urbanisation and the impacts of climate change are increasing the pressure to accelerate climate adaptation measures in fast-growing secondary cities in Mexico and South Africa. Adaptation efforts in both countries are affected by lacking capacities of cities and improvable urban development instruments. Against this background, the project works with two cities to support their transformation towards a more climate-resilient and pro-poor urban development by building on capacity development, improved mainstreaming of climate adaptation into planning processes, and the implementation of small-scale, easily replicable adaptation measures in public spaces of disadvantaged neighbourhoods. The project enables strong mechanisms of peer-to-peer learning and scaling-up between the project&#xb4;s partner cities, mentor, and transfer cities as well as national ministries relevant for climate change adaptation and urban development.</narrative>
  </description>
